    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "musig: invalidate output if pubnonce/aggnonce parsing fails",
    "user": {
      "login": "amartya1523",
      "id": 133855728,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOB_p58A",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/133855728?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/amartya1523",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "`musig_pubnonce_parse` and `musig_aggnonce_parse` return 0 on invalid input but leave the output object untouched. Every other parse function in the library (`ec_pubkey_parse`, `xonly_pubkey_parse`, the ECDSA signature parsers, `silentpayments_recipient_label_parse` and `musig_partial_sig_parse`) clears its output first, so a failed parse leaves an object that is rejected when used.\n\nWithout that, if the object already holds a nonce (e.g. a coordinator parsing incoming nonces into a reused array, as the test vectors do), the old nonce survives a failed parse and is accepted by `nonce_agg` / `nonce_process` without any error. If the object was never initialized, a later load reads uninitialized memory.\n\nCommits:\n- clear the output right after the `nonce != NULL` check, as `ec_pubkey_parse` does, so it is also cleared when `in66` is NULL\n- test that a failed parse (and a NULL `in66`) leaves a zeroed object that serialize and `nonce_agg` / `nonce_process` reject. An all-zero aggnonce is valid (infinity), so that test uses a bad prefix byte. These checks fail without the first commit.\n- `partial_sig_parse` cleared only after both ARG_CHECKs, so move its memset up the same way\n- document \"If not, it's set to an invalid value\" for the three musig parsers, matching `xonly_pubkey_parse`\n\nThis is narrower than #1850: it doesn't propose a general clear-on-failure rule, it only makes the musig parsers behave like the other parsers.",
