        }
      ],
      "message": "musig: invalidate nonce output if pubnonce/aggnonce parsing fails\n\nEvery other parse function in the library (ec_pubkey_parse,\nxonly_pubkey_parse, the ECDSA signature parsers,\nsilentpayments_recipient_label_parse and musig_partial_sig_parse)\nclears its output object before parsing, so that a failed parse leaves\nan object that is rejected when it is used later.\n\nmusig_pubnonce_parse and musig_aggnonce_parse return 0 but leave the\noutput untouched instead. If the object was not initialized, a later\nload reads uninitialized memory. If it holds an earlier nonce, for\nexample when a coordinator parses incoming nonces into a reused array,\nthat stale nonce stays valid and is accepted by nonce_agg and\nnonce_process without any error.\n\nClear the output right after checking that it is non-NULL, as\nec_pubkey_parse and xonly_pubkey_parse do, so that it is also cleared\nif in66 is NULL.",
